<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; connect-src 'none'; img-src 'none'; font-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-src 'none'">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>S122 — Supported Linux promotion rehearsal</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
  <script src="model.js" defer></script>
  <script src="app.js" defer></script>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <p id="training-banner" class="banner">Training rehearsal - synthetic data - not a live Azure result</p>
    <h1>S122: Choose a supported Linux promotion path</h1>
    <p>Assess a fictional candidate, explicitly promote it, and inspect fixed crossing-journey receipts.
      Nothing deploys, changes Azure settings or makes application/network requests.</p>
    <section aria-labelledby="constraints-heading">
      <h2 id="constraints-heading">Hosting constraints, not native proof</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Linux code:</strong> choose a reviewed manual swap or an explicitly controlled
          deployment/swap pipeline. Native auto-swap is unsupported.</li>
        <li><strong>Windows code:</strong> auto-swap is documented for eligible code-slot configurations;
          that does not confer support on Linux. Windows is not rehearsed here.</li>
        <li><strong>Web App for Containers:</strong> native auto-swap is also unsupported; see source S123.</li>
        <li>Deployment slots require a supported Standard, Premium or Isolated plan.
          This fictional Standard example is not an approved native SKU, region or resource.</li>
        <li>Two slots share the same <strong>two plan workers</strong>. Adding a slot, changing routing or
          swapping content does not add compute, capacity isolation or a separate failure domain.</li>
        <li>Production is the target. Review effective target settings, meaningful readiness,
          compatible state and overlap headroom. Default swap warm-up accepts any HTTP response
          unless acceptable statuses are specified; this fixture requires HTTP 200 plus all gates.</li>
        <li>Native swaps recycle former production workers and can abandon long operations.
          Keeping the old slot is not draining protection. Continuation below is fictional application data.</li>
        <li>Zero-percent routing is not access control. Slot-bound settings do not follow content.
          Managed identities, domain and scale settings are not treated as content-swapped settings.</li>
        <li>No swap-with-preview capability is exercised or qualified. Site authentication restricts
          preview in the documented workflow; no Linux preview claim is needed for the chosen path.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="operator-heading">
      <h2 id="operator-heading">Operator controls</h2>
      <p>Use Tab, arrow keys, Enter or Space. Six archived runs maximum. Reload starts a new
        in-memory lesson; reset keeps this page's history. All numbers are teaching assumptions.</p>
      <form id="lesson-form" novalidate>
        <label for="promotion-path">Linux promotion path</label>
        <select id="promotion-path" name="promotionPath" aria-describedby="auto-swap-limit">
          <option value="manual">Reviewed manual slot swap (rehearsal)</option>
          <option value="pipeline">Controlled deployment/swap pipeline (rehearsal)</option>
          <option value="native-auto-swap" disabled>Native auto-swap — unsupported on Linux</option>
        </select>
        <p id="auto-swap-limit">Native auto-swap is unavailable on Linux and Web App for Containers.
          A pipeline calling a supported swap explicitly is not native auto-swap.</p>
        <label for="fixture-choice">Fixed teaching fixture</label>
        <select id="fixture-choice" name="fixtureChoice">
          <option value="healthy">Prepared candidate with durable continuation</option>
          <option value="warmup-503">Warm-up responds HTTP 503</option>
          <option value="config-mismatch">Effective target configuration is wrong</option>
          <option value="overlap-deficit">Shared-plan overlap exceeds capacity</option>
          <option value="recycle-loss">Former worker loses long-running work</option>
          <option value="missing-observation">Two journey observations are missing</option>
        </select>
        <label for="journey-budget">Original journey budget (teaching ms)</label>
        <input id="journey-budget" name="journeyBudget" type="text" inputmode="numeric"
          value="250" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="budget-help">
        <p id="budget-help">An unpadded decimal integer from 100 to 500. This does not change any fixed request.</p>
        <button id="assess-candidate" type="submit">1. Assess candidate</button>
      </form>
      <div class="actions">
        <button id="promote-candidate" type="button" disabled>2. Promote (rehearsal)</button>
        <button id="measure-journeys" type="button" disabled>3. Measure fixed journeys</button>
        <button id="request-rollback" type="button" disabled>Request fictional rollback</button>
        <button id="reset-lesson" type="button">Reset current controls; retain history</button>
      </div>
      <p id="lesson-error" role="alert" tabindex="-1" hidden></p>
      <p id="lesson-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready to assess. No candidate has been exposed.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="state-heading">
      <h2 id="state-heading">Synthetic current state</h2>
      <p id="phase-label" data-phase="idle">idle</p>
      <dl>
        <dt>Fixed hosting / slots / compute</dt><dd>Linux code / production + staging / 2 shared plan workers</dd>
        <dt>Fictional content placement</dt><dd id="content-placement">production: old-v1; staging: candidate-v2</dd>
        <dt>Desired new-admission route</dt><dd id="desired-route">old-v1</dd>
        <dt>Observed migration</dt><dd id="observed-route">No crossing journeys observed</dd>
        <dt>Former production workers</dt><dd id="worker-state">Not swapped</dd>
      </dl>
      <ul id="readiness-gates"><li>Not assessed</li></ul>
      <p id="current-result">No run measured; no success percentage.</p>
      <table>
        <caption>Fixed synthetic receipts, not HTTP calls</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Journey</th><th scope="col">Observed versions</th>
          <th scope="col">Receipt and original budget</th><th scope="col">Outcome / reason</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody id="journey-rows"></tbody>
      </table>
      <ol id="action-trace"></ol>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="history-heading">
      <h2 id="history-heading">Retained run history</h2>
      <p id="history-count">0 / 6 archived runs</p>
      <ol id="run-history"></ol>
      <p id="aggregate-result">0 attempted transitions; no transition success percentage.</p>
      <p>Passing a safety gate or old-only request is not migration. Unknown started transitions
        stay in the denominator. Rollback cannot erase failures. A small correlated synthetic
        sample cannot establish native continuity, five-nines transition reliability or uptime.</p>
    </section>
    <footer>
      <p>Source: README S122; backlog D-S122; portable A-S122; packet SC-S122.
        B-S122, C062, C064 and the native/source-parent acceptance remain incomplete.</p>
      <p>Microsoft educational material is provided AS IS, with no endorsement or SLA claim.
        This lesson does not grant a license to source material or use Microsoft trademarks as certification.</p>
      <p><a href="README.txt">Lesson instructions and limits</a></p>
    </footer>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
